    "chapterDelineation": "Chapter"
  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 28,
    "summary": "The wicked flee when no man pursues—Whoever walks uprightly will be saved—A faithful man will abound with blessings.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "The wicked flee when no man pursueth: but the righteous are bold as a lion.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Lev. 26:17; Amos 9:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "2 Ne. 9:40."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the transgression of a land many are the princes thereof: but by a man of understanding and knowledge the state thereof shall be prolonged.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 40
          },
          {
            "start": 92,
            "end": 95
          },
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 123
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A poor man that oppresseth the poor is like a sweeping rain which leaveth no food.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Oppression."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 43
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They that forsake the law praise the wicked: but such as keep the law contend with them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Evil men understand not judgment: but they that seek the Lord understand all things.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "D&C 88:67."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 84
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Better is the poor that walketh in his uprightness, than he that is perverse in his ways, though he be rich.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "Prov. 10:9; 19:1."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 9
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 67
          },
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 83
          },
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 102
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso keepeth the law is a wise son: but he that is a companion of riotous men shameth his father.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "OR gluttonous. Luke 15:13 (12–13). TG Rioting and Reveling."
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "TG Shame."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 24
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that by usury and unjust gain increaseth his substance, he shall gather it for him that will pity the poor.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Usury."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "Alma 11:20."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that turneth away his ear from hearing the law, even his prayer shall be abomination.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "Prov. 29:18; D&C 88:35 (34–35)."
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "Ps. 109:7; Moro. 7:6 (6–7)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso causeth the righteous to go astray in an evil way, he shall fall himself into his own pit: but the upright shall have good things in possession.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "TG Justice."
          },
          {
            "start": 92,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "Prov. 26:27; 1 Ne. 22:14."
          },
          {
            "start": 129,
            "end": 135,
            "text": "Gen. 24:1; Matt. 6:33."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 129,
            "end": 135
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The rich man is wise in his own conceit; but the poor that hath understanding searcheth him out.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 53,
            "text": "Alma 32:12 (12–13); D&C 104:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 15
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When righteous men do rejoice, there is great glory: but when the wicked rise, a man is hidden.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "Prov. 11:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 18
          },
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 39
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that covereth his sins shall not prosper: but whoso confesseth and forsaketh them shall have mercy.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "Job 31:33; Luke 12:2 (1–3); 1 Jn. 1:10; D&C 1:3; 121:37 (36–38)."
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "TG Confession."
          },
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "TG Repent."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 84
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Happy is the man that feareth alway: but he that hardeneth his heart shall fall into mischief.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "TG Reverence."
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "TG Hardheartedness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 8
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As a roaring lion, and a ranging bear; so is a wicked ruler over the poor people.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "Ezek. 22:25."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The prince that wanteth understanding is also a great oppressor: but he that hateth covetousness shall prolong his days.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "TG Covet."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 40
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 68
          },
          {
            "start": 111,
            "end": 114
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A man that doeth violence to the blood of any person shall flee to the pit; let no man stay him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "Alma 1:13 (13–14)."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "OR flee to the sepulchre (grave); i.e., flee to death."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso walketh uprightly shall be saved: but he that is perverse in his ways shall fall at once.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "TG Walking with God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 54
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that tilleth his land shall have plenty of bread: but he that followeth after vain persons shall have poverty enough.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 93
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A faithful man shall abound with blessings: but he that maketh haste to be rich shall not be innocent.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "TG Haste."
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "TG Treasure."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "To have respect of persons is not good: for for a piece of bread that man will transgress.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Prov. 24:23; James 2:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "Ezek. 13:19."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "TG Bread."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 29
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 69
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that hasteth to be rich hath an evil eye, and considereth not that poverty shall come upon him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 31
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that rebuketh a man afterwards shall find more favour than he that flattereth with the tongue.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "Prov. 27:5."
          },
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "TG Flatter."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso robbeth his father or his mother, and saith, It is no transgression; the same is the companion of a destroyer.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 56
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 86
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that is of a proud heart stirreth up strife: but he that putteth his trust in the Lord shall be made fat.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "Prov. 13:10; 2 Ne. 28:12 (12–13)."
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "TG Strife."
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "D&C 11:12; 84:116."
          },
          {
            "start": 99,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "IE prosperous."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that trusteth in his own heart is a fool: but whoso walketh wisely, he shall be delivered.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Trust Not in the Arm of Flesh."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that giveth unto the poor shall not lack: but he that hideth his eyes shall have many a curse.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "TG Almsgiving; Poor; Welfare."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When the wicked rise, men hide themselves: but when they perish, the righteous increase.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "D&C 98:9."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "nextChapterId": "proverbs29",
